<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Slav Rising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">983</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Slavic uprising of 983</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Slav Rising was a revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polabian-slavs">Polabian Slavs</a>, led by the Lutician tribes, against German rule east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> in 983. The rebels destroyed the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havelberg">Havelberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and drove out the margraves of the Northern March. German control of the region was lost for more than a century, and Slavic paganism revived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-slav-rising.jpg" alt="Great Slav Rising" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Skäpperöd · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lutizenbund.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
